{
  "example": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.agent_config`\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.with_agent`\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`\n\nThis Bedrock configuration selects a model, AWS profile, and region for the\ndomain's cache:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse trust_but_verify::agent::AgentConfig;\nuse trust_but_verify::agent::BedrockConfig;\nuse trust_but_verify::domain::ValidationCache;\n\nlet config = AgentConfig::Bedrock(\n    BedrockConfig::new(\"us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5\".into())\n        .aws_profile(\"development\".into())\n        .region(\"us-east-1\".into()),\n);\nlet cache = ValidationCache::with_agent(config);\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The example is concrete. It builds a Bedrock `AgentConfig` with a model, AWS profile and region, then calls `ValidationCache::with_agent(config)`. The expected behavior is that the configuration selects the agent for that domain's cache.\n\nThe only supplied {test} reference is `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted]`. It uses the same inputs as the example: the model `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5`, profile `development` and region `us-east-1`. It checks these outcomes:\n- **Empty cache.** After `ValidationCache::with_agent(config.clone())`, the test asserts the cache's `outlines` are empty and `sources` is `None`. This matches \"creates an empty cache\" in `requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`.\n- **Agent selected for the domain.** It asserts that the cache's `agent` is present. It also asserts that a clone of the domain shares the same agent through `Arc::ptr_eq`, and that the agent's `config` equals the supplied configuration.\n- **Use by a criterion.** It runs a criterion through `validation::refresh_evidence` on the domain with the agent attached. The `Question(false)` criterion is deterministic, so this also matches `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.with_agent`, where a cache with an agent still supports deterministic criteria. It asserts that the criterion's output is false.\n- **Not persisted.** It serializes the stored record. It asserts the record has no `backend` key and that its text contains neither `development` nor `claude-sonnet`. This matches \"The SDK does not persist it.\"\n\nI found two weak points, and neither is a gap against the example's text:\n- **Builder methods.** The equality check compares the cached config with a config built by the same builder calls, so it cannot catch a builder that drops the profile or region. Those builders are tested separately in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#mod[tests]/fn[backend_builders_set_only_the_requested_fields]`, and they fall under `agent_config`, which the example only cites.\n- **Deferred backend setup.** The test does not assert that the lazily created provider is still uninitialized. The example does not state deferral. It belongs to `requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`, which the same test also references.\n\nThe test covers the example's scenario and each outcome it states, so I judge the tests adequate.",
  "references": "7c7524ee8e51af918c33943dcb55e9936d8e326b278323071bdbeabdfe57c6a0",
